@startuml
!include ../11-bmc/_style.iuml
title Three ways to build WaslaBid as a company
legend top left
|= |= A. Capital-light SaaS |= B. Tender-data lender |=<#D5F5E3> C. SaaS first, lender option (recommended) |
| **What it is** | Document 11 as planned | Licensed debt-crowdfunding or SME finance company that finances verified private awards | Run A; build the two cheap data foundations; decide on B at year 3 with real volume |
| **Capital needed** | About SAR 185k over 3 years | SAR 5M+ licence capital, plus a warehouse credit line | SAR 185k now; B money only if the gate passes |
| **Licence** | None | SAMA finance company licence | None until the year-3 decision |
| **Team** | Founder plus 1 to 2 Saudi hires | Full-time founders, credit and compliance team | Founder part-time until gate 1, full-time after 10 tenants |
| **5-year value** | SAR 10M to 20M | Venture-scale if SAR 2B to 4B is financed a year | A's value, plus the option on B |
| **Main risk** | Slow sales | Credit losses; competes with Lendo and Tameed | Volume never reaches the year-3 gate |
| **Exit** | Strategic sale: Reference App, ERP vendor, lender | Fintech IPO or sale | Either |
|<#FCF3CF> **Verdict** |<#FCF3CF> Safe, small |<#FCF3CF> Big, but not a first step |<#82E0AA> Keeps the upside at the cost of A |
endlegend
@enduml
